### For the VS Code "REST Client" extension. Paste the accessToken from login into @token.
@base = http://localhost:5000/api
@token = paste-the-access-token-here
@csrf = {{csrfToken.response.body.csrfToken}}

### Run this first: the CSRF token for this session (every POST and PATCH sends it back)
# @name csrfToken
GET {{base}}/csrf-token

### Register (the first account becomes admin)
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
x-csrf-token: {{csrf}}

{ "username": "kevin", "password": "longPassword1" }

### Login: returns an access token, sets the refresh cookie
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
x-csrf-token: {{csrf}}

{ "username": "kevin", "password": "longPassword1" }

### New token pair from the refresh cookie
POST {{base}}/auth/refresh
x-csrf-token: {{csrf}}

### Any logged-in user
GET {{base}}/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin only
GET {{base}}/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Admin only: change a role
PATCH {{base}}/admin/users/2/role
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-csrf-token: {{csrf}}

{ "role": "admin" }

### Logout (revokes the refresh token)
POST {{base}}/auth/logout
x-csrf-token: {{csrf}}
